# hover_alt.scn — airborne ALTITUDE_HOLD hover (legacy firmware / emu_vehicle)
# 空中 ALTITUDE_HOLD ホバー（旧ファーム / emu_vehicle）
#
# Sticks are raw 12-bit ADC, 0..4095, centre 2048 (firmware treats them as ADC;
# the "0..1000" comment in controller_comm.hpp is stale).
# スティックは raw 12bit ADC（0..4095, 中央 2048）。
#
# Throttle mapping (verified): open-loop T = clamp((raw-2048)/2048, 0, 1); thrust =
# T * MAX_TOTAL_THRUST (0.672 N). weight = 0.363 N → lift-off needs T>0.540 (raw>3155).
# Centre raw 2048 → T=0 (idle) AND the ALT_HOLD hold deadzone (|norm|<0.1).
# スロットル写像（裏取り済）: 開ループ T=clamp((raw-2048)/2048,0,1)、thrust=T*0.672N。
# 荷重0.363N → 離陸は T>0.540(raw>3155)。raw2048 は T=0 かつ ALT_HOLD 保持 deadzone。
#
# alt token: the OPTIONAL 4th rc field. alt=1 sets CTRL_FLAG_ALT_MODE(0x08) →
# ALTITUDE_HOLD on the firmware side. '+' = immediately after the previous event.
# alt トークン: rc の任意 4番目。alt=1 で CTRL_FLAG_ALT_MODE(0x08)→ALTITUDE_HOLD。
#
# rc: <t> rc <thr> <roll> <pitch> <yaw> <arm> [hold_ms] [rate_hz] [alt]
#
# ARM TIMING (critical): the firmware accepts ARM only on a RISING EDGE of
# CTRL_FLAG_ARM AND only while FlightState == IDLE (main.cpp:302-305; requestArm()
# returns false SILENTLY otherwise — stampfly_state.cpp:67). An ARM edge before IDLE
# is consumed and never re-fires (s_prev_arm_flag latches), so the craft never arms.
# IDLE is set at the very end of boot, and boot starts LATE in virtual time:
#   t=0..3 s   app_main's vTaskDelay(3000) "USB connect" delay (main.cpp:449)
#   t~3.5 s    Phase 1 starts; fixed 5 s settle (main.cpp:521 SETTLE_TIME_MS)
#   t~8.5 s    Phase 1 complete; Phase 2 sensor stabilisation (exits early ~1 s)
#   t~9.5 s    "Phase 3: System ready!" → setFlightState(IDLE) (main.cpp:955→963)
# So IDLE ~= 9.5 s. Phase A stays disarmed 13 s so the single ARM edge in Phase B
# lands well past IDLE. (Do NOT patch out the 3 s delay — SIL runs firmware UNMODIFIED.)
# アーム受理は CTRL_FLAG_ARM 立上りエッジ かつ FlightState==IDLE のときのみ（外れると
# requestArm は無言 false）。IDLE 前のエッジは消費され再発火しない。boot は app_main 冒頭の
# vTaskDelay(3000)（USB待ち）で 3s 遅れて始まり、Phase1 固定5s + Phase2 → IDLE は仮想 t≈9.5s。
# ゆえに位相Aは 13s 待つ。3s 遅延は SIL の Code Identity 原則によりパッチしない。
#
#  <t>  ch   <thr> <roll> <pitch> <yaw> <arm> <hold_ms> <rate_hz> <alt>
   0    rc   2048  2048   2048    2048  0     13000     50              # A: disarmed 13 s — clear boot→IDLE (~9.5 s) before ARM edge
   +    rc   2048  2048   2048    2048  1     1000      50              # B: ARM rising edge (now in IDLE), throttle centre = T=0 (motors idle) 1 s
   +    rc   3310  2048   2048    2048  1     2600      50              # C: STABILIZE gentle take-off — T=0.616, firmware commands 0.414 N; the Plant's 1/1.12 efficiency yields ≈0.370 N → net ≈+0.007 N → climb ≈0.2 m/s². Measured: reaches ≈0.62 m in 2.6 s (peak ~0.68 m), well under the 1.4 m ToF ceiling. The physics integrates at 4000 Hz LOCKED to virtual time (cea0d8c), so the ToF distance and the ESKF velocity advance at the SAME rate the firmware predicts — the ESKF keeps a clean ToF lock through the climb (ALT capture reads the true ~0.62 m, not a diverged value).
   +    rc   2048  2048   2048    2048  1     16000     50        1     # D: switch to ALT_HOLD (alt=1) WHILE AIRBORNE with a good lock → captureAltitude(current) holds it; centre stick unlocks hold. Hover 16 s.
   +    rc   1000  2048   2048    2048  1     2500      50        1     # E: descent stick (norm -0.51 → -0.14 m/s) → setpoint sinks toward MIN 0.10 m, 2.5 s
   +    rc   2048  2048   2048    2048  0     1000      50              # F: DISARM, motors cut 1 s
#
# REAL-FLIGHT-STYLE take-off: a gentle STABILIZE lift-off FIRST (so the ESKF gets a clean
# ToF lock and LandingHandler registers take-off while airborne), THEN hand to ALT_HOLD,
# which captures the CURRENT altitude — the real-flight sequence. Two SIL-plant fixes make
# this faithful (NOT firmware changes — the firmware flew on real hardware):
#   1. Plant 1/1.12 thrust efficiency (66752df) matching the firmware's HOVER_THRUST_CORRECTION,
#      so the hover command yields actual mg (no 1.12 over-thrust). Without it the craft
#      over-climbs to ~6 m.
#   2. Fixed-timestep physics LOCKED to virtual time at 4000 Hz (cea0d8c). Previously the
#      Plant was stepped once per scheduler clock-event (~3x per 2.5 ms), so physics ran ~3x
#      faster than virtual time — the apparent climb was 1.75 m/s² (= true 0.196 × 3²) and the
#      ESKF saw a ToF that moved 3x faster than its own velocity prediction, so its accel bias
#      diverged (the old "ESKF vertical divergence / takeoff handoff" blocker). With the fix
#      ToF and the ESKF advance at the same rate and the lock stays clean. See
#      simulator/sil/docs/plant_timebase_bug.md.
# 実飛行流の離陸: まず STABILIZE で穏やかに離陸し空中で ToF ロック確立→ALT_HOLD が現在高度を
# キャプチャ。忠実化は SIL プラント側の2修正（firmware は無改変）: ①推力効率 1/1.12(66752df)で
# hover 指令が実 mg を生む ②物理を仮想時間にロックした 4000Hz 固定刻み(cea0d8c)。以前は物理が
# 約3倍速で「ESKF鉛直発散」blocker を生んでいたが、これで ToF と ESKF が同レートで進み解消。
#
# Expectation (MEASURED with both fixes; tune from trajectory.csv `alt`, NOT control gains):
#   C: alt rises to ~0.62 m (leaves the ground; cf. hover_espnow at T=0.50 stays grounded).
#   D: ALT_HOLD captures the current altitude (~0.62 m, clamped [0.10,3.0] m) and HOLDS it;
#      raw2048 is inside the ±0.1 deadzone → climb_cmd=0 → setpoint frozen. The COMMANDED
#      thrust settles near the hover feedforward 0.407 N (= mg×1.12); the Plant's 1/1.12
#      efficiency turns that into actual mg=0.363 N → hover (vz≈0). So the firmware-side
#      thrust log reads ~0.406 N, NOT 0.363 N — the efficiency, not the VEL PID, removes the
#      1.12 factor.
#   E: controlled descent; setpoint sinks toward MIN 0.10 m.
#   F: motors cut, craft lands (truth alt → ~0.01 m).
#
# TUNING: raw3310 / 2600 ms are the working values (peak ~0.68 m, ALT_HOLD holds ~0.62 m).
#   If C overshoots MAX 3.0 m or stays under MIN 0.10 m, adjust raw(3180..3400) and hold_ms
#   from the `alt` column. NEVER touch HOVER_THRUST_CORRECTION — the closed loop absorbs it
#   (hover_resume.md §1). The 4000 Hz virtual-time-locked physics (cea0d8c) is REQUIRED for
#   the climb / ToF / ESKF to be physically consistent (plant_timebase_bug.md).
